  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1-\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\ (3+5\\text{i})(1-\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 3-3\\text{i}+5\\text{i}-5{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 3+5+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 8+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n8=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and $q=2.$",
